pinned CDN only when this feature is opened. Same-origin tabs also use BroadcastChannel. Hosts own the simulation and guests send inputs. Both pilots share convoy and score; each has separate hull, replacement helicopters and flares.\n\nThe bundled AI Hub session client implements shared-world protocol 1. Sessions automatically connect and ready, respect the countdown, support a server with no local player, and report a tied team score. No external signaling is used inside AI Hub. Its menu and round lifecycle own session entry/exit.\n\n## Developer hangar\n\nPause → Developer Hangar. Live sliders expose speed, enemy traffic, damage, convoy armor, weapon power and simulation speed. Tools include invincibility, sector skip, carrier spawn, full repair, clear hostiles, victory inspection and reset to defaults. Run upgrades reset on a new sortie.\n\n## Build and verification\n\n`npm run build` rebuilds the single HTML from the source modules and editable template.\n\n`npm test --silent` is the consolidated quiet verification command. It runs gameplay, controller/touch, offline audio, file boot, standalone networking and the unmodified AI Hub harness. It prints failures and one count. Browser executables are the installed Playwright 1.63 browsers. Every server binds OS-assigned `127.0.0.1` ports and shuts down after its test.\n\nThe saved visual captures in `tests/` were inspected for composition and legibility at 1920×1080 and portrait phone size. They use WebGL 2 because this machine'\"'s headless WebGPU compositor captures a blank canvas even when the game state and GPU renderer run. \"'`tests/visual-check.py` is the capture implementation. Test reports and complete scripted playthrough states are also in `tests/`.\n\nThe title draw used Python `secrets.randbelow(50)`; `title-draw.json` records the result. `report.json`, the root `exit-interview.json` and the in-game About screen hold the requested source and feedback information. Usage is added on import.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\nr=json.loads(pathlib.Path('../exit-interview.json').read_text())\nassert set(r)=={'sourceInformation','testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback','aiHub'}\nassert [len(r[k]) for k in ['testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback']]==[4,6,4]\nassert r['sourceInformation']['usage']=='added on import'\nprint('Exit interview JSON validated')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Exit interview JSON validated\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='main.js';s=open(p).read();s=s.replace('ship.mesh.rotation.y = ship.face === 1 ? 0 : Math.PI;', 'ship.mesh.rotation.y=0;ship.mesh.scale.x=Math.abs(ship.mesh.scale.x)*ship.face;')\ns=s.replace('e.mesh.rotation.y = e.face === 1 ? 0 : Math.PI;', 'e.mesh.rotation.y=0;e.mesh.scale.x=Math.abs(e.mesh.scale.x)*e.face;')\ns=s.replace('e.mesh.rotation.y = data.face === -1 ? Math.PI : 0;', 'e.mesh.rotation.y=0;e.mesh.scale.x=Math.abs(e.mesh.scale.x)*(data.face||1);')\ns=s.replace('e = { ...data, mesh };\\\\n\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tmesh.position', 'e = { ...data, mesh };\\\\n\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tif(data.type===\\\"enemy\\\"&&data.kind\"'!==\"jet\")mesh.scale.setScalar(.85);'\"\\\\n\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tmesh.position')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='index.template.html';s=open(p).read().replace('#bossHud{display:none;', '#bossHud{background:#103137ed;padding:10px 16px;display:none;').replace('#titleScreen .stack{max-width:380px}', '#titleScreen .stack{max-width:380px}#titleScreen .row button{white-space:nowrap;font-size:14px;padding:10px 12px}')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/visual-check.py';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"page.evaluate('__game.boss();\\\", \\\"page.mouse.move(1700,400);page.evaluate('__game.boss();\\\");open(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/run_tests.py';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"'tests/hub-check.py']\\\", \\\"'tests/hub-check.py','tests/visual-check.py']\\\");open(p,'w').write(s)\np='report.json';import json,pathlib\nr=json.loads(pathlib.Path(p).read_text());r['testingFeedback'][0]='5 issues caught by testing: a guest snapshot exception, three HUD contrast problems and cockpit visibility when facing left. All fixed.'\npathlib.Path(p).write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\\\\n');pathlib.Path('../exit-interview.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nbiome format --write main.js > /dev/null\nnpm run build && npm test --silent\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
